#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""dt-install-drift — is what B-CREDENTIALS-PRIVATE-REPO installed on THIS box still exactly what
was reviewed and installed, and is it actually in force? Pre-audit §2.2 item 10 (C-18). Runs as
root, DAILY (the spec's cadence), on each box; a failure pages through the box's failure unit
(staging: dt-unit-failure@ → a system alert naming Infra Claude; Helsinki: agent-unit-failure@ →
the crew channel).

WHAT IT COMPARES AGAINST — the INSTALLED sha, not the branch head (fresh-reader r1): the install
records the reviewed sha it installed from in INSTALLED_SHA. Every file is hashed against its blob
AT THAT SHA, so a change sitting in review is not "drift". A committed change that is NOT yet
installed is reported as PENDING, and pages only once the commit that made it is over a week old.
INSTALLED_SHA's format (r3 S6 — two install flows own some of the same Helsinki files):
    <sha>                  the default: every file was installed from this sha
    <sha> <repo path>      an override: THIS file was installed from that sha (the last line wins)
so a flow that installs one file records its own sha for it, and neither flow's install reads as
the other's drift.

⛔ ROOT RUNS NO GIT. The blob ids are read by the account that OWNS the repo (deploy on staging,
   langston on Helsinki); root re-hashes the installed file itself (sha1 of "blob <len>\\0<bytes>").
⚠️ STATED RESIDUAL: the ids come from the repo owner's git, so an owner who could edit the repo AND
   an installed file could make them agree. On staging that owner is deploy, who is root until
   #1102 — this detects accidents and hand edits; it is not a tamper boundary.

Every line it prints is one fact; anything but OK/PENDING fails the run:
    OK       <path> = <repo path> at <installed sha>
    DRIFT    <path> differs from <repo path> at <installed sha>
    MISSING  <path>
    PERM     <path> mode/owner is X, wanted Y
    PENDING  <repo path> changed on the branch after the install (fails once over 7 days old)
    UNIT     a unit or timer is not in force as installed (reload, enablement, extra drop-ins)
    STATE    a runtime fact that must hold (a dt-api page, a setter marker, accounts, keys, sudo)
    SOURCE   the committed source is unreadable or stale — mirror health, not drift
EXIT: 0 = nothing but OK/PENDING · 1 = anything else.
"""
